{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792488695,"nonce":"fQjTedbNmWooDS1TAY3inBuW62s=","title":"Opt-in image residency for scrollable divs","message":"Add virtualizeImages:Bool on Div, false by default. Under an opted-in scroll container, offscreen Image uses release reloadable decoded pixels while keeping layout dimensions and compressed source. Reentry restores the pixels and the previous shrink cap. All uses of a shared Bitmap participate; an unmanaged or visible use keeps it resident, and escaped raw slots, brushes/canvas and mesh consumers conservatively pin the source. A nested explicit false can opt out.\n\nManage SVG atlas residency without deleting caller-owned parsed documents. Repack the renderer-owned image atlas at a smaller capacity when a managed image enters/leaves view or is removed. Invalidate CanvasPainter atlas revisions and retained-frame damage when coordinates change. Distinguish native bitmap slot generations so an atlas cache never substitutes a previously freed image.\n\nBaseline standalone Ashui probe: after image records drop from 1 to 0 while scrolled away, decoded pixels remain 1,600,000 bytes and atlas 1,048,576 bytes even after collection. With opt-in, decoded pixels drop to zero and atlas becomes 262,144 bytes (256x256 RGBA floor); reentry restores pixels. No extension VM is loaded in the probe.\n\nVerify default-off, repeated scrolling/reentry with pixel equality, shared images/brushes/raw slots, nested and reactive changes, dimension stability, SVG-only eviction, owner/tree cleanup and production Markdown scroll snapshots. No duplicate Cargo targets or native changes are needed.","files":null}]}